# track's atomic-write temp files (auto-removed; ignored as a safety net). Scoped to
# the tracker pair's own names (B119): a repo-wide *.tmp.* / *.data.* glob silently
# untracked legitimate files like app.data.json or video.tmp.mp4.
tracker.md.tmp.*
tracker.html.tmp.*
tracker.md.data.*
tracker-hwm.tmp.*

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Claude Code worktrees (live parallel-session checkouts — never commit them)
.claude/worktrees/

# Claude Code personal settings — machine-local, never committed. The glob also covers
# the harness's atomic-write temp siblings (settings.local.json.tmp.<pid>.<hex>), which
# otherwise show as untracked noise and can race `git add -A` into an abort (B128).
.claude/settings.local.json*

# Claude Code personal instructions. CLAUDE.local.md loads after CLAUDE.md in every session and
# is meant to stay personal (the Claude Code docs say to gitignore it; nothing does so on its
# own). Unanchored on purpose: Claude Code also reads a CLAUDE.local.md in any subdirectory,
# and a root-only /CLAUDE.local.md would leave those one `git add -A` away from history.
CLAUDE.local.md
